Here is the code for an odd number.

We know odd numbers give a remainder of 1 when we divide by 2. 

Therefore supper we had a number  n, and we wanted to see if n was odd. We could divide n by 2 and check for a remainder.

n = int(input("What number do you want to test ?"))
  if n % 2 == 1:
  print("Odd")
  else:
  print("Even")


What if we had a list and we wanted to see which numbers within that list were odd

x =  list(map(int, input().split()))

odd = [i for i in x if i % 2 != 0]
print(odd)

Alternative code for listing odd numbers:
odd = [i for i in x if i % 2 == 1]






